// runtime.sets: the `runtime` superdomain.
//
// Runtime concepts (RUNTIME.md). A runtime domain isn't data: it is a
// tagged domain that is unique and equal only to itself (VM-PRES-3). Its
// one member stands in for the concept; it is never serialized or checked
// as data. Tags are the reserved atoms of RT-1.

Phi in base
Tagged in base
U in base

Async({T sub U}): Tagged(RuntimeAsync, T)
// Function tags the pair of its domains, so Function(Phi, String) and
// Function(Phi, Integer) stay distinct.
Function({A sub U}, {R sub U}): Tagged(RuntimeFunction, { (A, R) })
Mutex = Tagged(RuntimeMutex, Phi)
Channel({T sub U}): Tagged(RuntimeChannel, T)
Handle = Tagged(RuntimeHandle, Phi)
